# Task Runner Instructions

> This file instructs the AI agent on how to execute tasks in this workspace.
> System Prompt reference: Load this when starting a task.

## Your Workflow

You must strictly follow this workflow when executing any task in this workspace:

### 1. Load Context First
Before editing any code, read the active task files:
- `tasks/current/TASK.md` (to understand requirements and acceptance criteria)
- `tasks/current/CONTEXT.md` (to know exactly which files you are allowed to read and edit)
- `PICKUP.md` (if resuming a session, to get the handover notes)

### 2. Respect Scope Boundaries
- **Only touch files listed in `tasks/current/CONTEXT.md` under "Relevant Files"**.
- Do NOT read or modify files listed under "DO NOT Touch".
- If you need to modify a file not listed in the context, stop and ask the user to add it to `CONTEXT.md` first.

### 3. Track Your Progress
As you work:
- Update `tasks/current/PROGRESS.md` at key milestones.
- Document design decisions made and code changes.
- Record any blockers or issues encountered.

### 4. Verification
- Only run the specific tests or check commands listed in `tasks/current/CONTEXT.md` under "Verification Commands".
- Do not run full test suites unless explicitly scoped.

### 5. Session Handoff
Before ending your turn or when completing the task:
- Update `PICKUP.md` with:
  - Concise summary of changes.
  - In-progress items.
  - Recommended next steps for the next agent.
- If the task is finished, move the task folder from `tasks/current/` to `tasks/completed/`.
